PROBLEM="Choose a C# project architecture when the user did not specify one (and structure accordingly)."
LEARNINGS="DEFAULT to CLEAN ARCHITECTURE when no architecture is specified - it's the mainstream modern ASP.NET default (Microsoft eShop reference, most templates): layered with the dependency rule pointing INWARD to a pure domain core. Switch only on a clear signal: rich domain rules/invariants -> DDD; many simple CRUD features -> Vertical Slice; explicit legacy/n-tier request -> Layered. Precedence: legacy request first, then rich-domain (DDD) over many-features (Vertical Slice)."
ERRORS="Do NOT leave the architecture unspecified/ad-hoc for a normal user; default to Clean. Do NOT pick Vertical Slice or DDD without a clear signal - Clean is the safe default."
TAGS="src:context7 lang:csharp area:architecture arch:default arch:clean"
REF_SRC="ArchChoice.cs"
